Aim: To study and implement the Agile software development lifecycle using Jira and understand DevOps pipeline integration.

Requirements:
- Internet connection
- Jira account
- Web browser
Procedure:
1. Open Google Chrome.
2. Visit Jira official website.
3. Sign up or log in using your account.
4. Create a new Jira project.
5. Select the Scrum or Kanban project template.
6. Enter a project name, for example, Student Management System.
7. Open the project dashboard.
8. Create tasks (issues) for the project:
   - User login
   - Registration
   - Dashboard development
   - Database connection
   - Testing
9. Assign tasks to different team members.
10. Set priorities and deadlines for each task.
11. Move tasks across the workflow:
    - To Do
    - In Progress
    - Done
12. Create a sprint if you selected Scrum.
13. Start the sprint and update the task status as work progresses.
14. Open the project reports to view progress.
15. Study how Jira can be integrated with GitHub and Jenkins to connect project management with development and deployment.
Expected Output: A Jira project is created successfully with tasks, team members, deadlines and workflow status.
